    "metaTitle": "Products for Home and Household Appliances",
    "metaDescription": "Eine weitere WordPress-Website",
    "body": "## CABLE TIES; CABLE FASTENING, MARKING AND IDENTIFICATION SOLUTIONS\n\nWith the heterogeneous demands their manifold uses and applications entail, home and household appliances often present a unique set of technical challenges.\n\nBIT offers custom solutions tailored to your company’s individual requirements without sacrificing strict conformity to international industry standards and specifications (such as UL 224, VW-1, UL 1441, DIN 40628, DIN 40621, etc.).\n\nYour request is no matter of rinse, wash, and repeat to us. Let us help you apply the right part to your appliance today!\n\nPARTS OFTEN USED FOR HOME APPLIANCES\n\nBP 125\n\nPolyolefin\n\nthin-wall, flame-retardant, flexible, halogen-free, practically non-flammable, UL-certified\n\nFlexible bundling, protection and color-coding of wires and cables.\n\n| Shrinking Rate: | 2:1\n\n| Certification: | UL 224\n\n| Temperature Range Min.: | -55 °C\n\n| Temperature Range Max.: | 125 °C\n\n### PVDF (KYNAR®)\n\nthin-wall, practically non-flammable, self-extinguishing, UL-certified, UV-resistant\n\nPerfect for applications that require both high mechanical and thermal resistance.\n\n| Shrinking Rate: | 2:1\n\n| Certification: | UL 224, 125°C, VW-1, 600V\n\n| Temperature Range Min.: | -55 °C\n\n| Temperature Range Max.: | +175 °C\n\n### Soft PVC\n\nflexible, self-extinguishing\n\nVery cost-effective, flexible PVC sleeve for bundling and insulating cables and Litz-type wires.\n\n| Temperature Range Min.: | -20 °C\n\n| Temperature Range Max.: | 85 °C\n\n### PA 6.6\n\nwith pre-punched fixing eye\n\nCable ties with fixing eye for secure fastening of cables and cable looms.\n\n| Temperature Range Min.: | -40 °C\n\n| Temperature Range Max.: | +85 °C",
