    "title": "Products for Mechanical and Plant Engineering",
    "metaTitle": "Products for Mechanical and Plant Engineering",
    "metaDescription": "Eine weitere WordPress-Website",
    "body": "## ELECTRICAL INSULATION; THERMAL, ABRASION AND VIBRATION PROTECTION\n\nProviding solutions for cable protection and harnessing to companies in machine construction as well as to those in mechanical and plant engineering has been a hallmark of our company since its formation.\n\nTechnical requirements in areas like agricultural, construction and industrial machinery are frequently exacting but can often be covered by standard products offering high abrasion, chemical or thermal resistance. Also in high demand are parts that allow for bundling components with large diameters or with diameters that vary widely in size. Of course, we will also gladly assist you should you require custom-made specialty items for your application.\n\nGet your machine going with parts from BIT!\n\nPARTS OFTEN USED IN MECHANICAL ENGINEERING\n\nBP 300\n\nPolyolefin\n\nthin-wall, flame-retardant, high shrink ratio, UL-certified\n\nDue to its improved shrink ratio, BP 300 can easily shrink around components that vary in size.\n\n| Shrinking Rate: | 3:1\n\n| Certification: | UL 224 (except clear-colored)\n\n| Temperature Range Min.: | -55 °C\n\n| Temperature Range Max.: | 135 °C\n\n### Polyolefin\n\nhigh shrink ratio, adhesive-lined, medium wall thickness, UV-resistant\n\nBPMW A provides excellent protection from moisture and adverse weather conditions.\n\n| Shrinking Rate: | 3:1\n\n| Temperature Range Min.: | -55 °C\n\n| Temperature Range Max.: | 110 °C\n\n### Polyester- and Polyolefin fibers\n\nflame-retardant, mesh weave, halogen-free\n\nBP HSF 125 braided heat-shrink tubing provides superior mechanical abrasion protection.\n\n| Shrinking Rate: | 2:1\n\n| Temperature Range Min.: | -40 °C\n\n| Temperature Range Max.: | 125 °C\n\n| Temperature Range Min.: | °C\n\n| Temperature Range Max.: | °C",
