    "metaTitle": "Products for Medical Technology and Engineering",
    "metaDescription": "Eine weitere WordPress-Website",
    "body": "## CERTIFIED SLEEVES AND TUBING FOR MEDICAL ENGINEERING\n\nQuality and reliability are obviously critical concerns in the medical sector; the demands placed on parts used for medtech applications are thus accordingly high.\n\nThis is why BIT partners up with leading companies worldwide to supply its clients in the medical sector with cutting-edge custom solutions and certified products. This includes, for instance, biocompatible material that comes with USP Class VI specification.\n\nContact us to receive the right treatment for your medtech issue!\n\nPARTS OFTEN USED IN THE MEDICAL SECTOR\n\nBPUTW\n\nPolyolefin\n\nthin-wall, flame-retardant, flexible, UL-certified, ultra-thin walled\n\nBPUTW ultra-thin walled tubing shrinks quickly around sensitive components providing an optimal fit.\n\n| Shrinking Rate: | 2:1\n\n| Certification: | UL 224 (except clear)\n\n| Temperature Range Min.: | -55 °C\n\n| Temperature Range Max.: | 125 °C\n\n### PTFE\n\nanti-adhesive, thin-wall, high chemical resistance, high temperature resistance, non-flammable\n\nHigh chemical, mechanical and thermal resistance are the hallmarks of this heat-shrink tube.\n\n| Shrinking Rate: | 2:1\n\n| Temperature Range Min.: | -67 °C\n\n| Temperature Range Max.: | 260 °C\n\n### VMQ\n\nhalogen-free, highly flexible, UL-certified\n\nFlexible high-quality insulation of electronic components with full UL certification.\n\n| Certification: | UL 224\n\n| Temperature Range Min.: | -50 °C\n\n| Temperature Range Max.: | 200 °C\n\n### Fiberglass with silicone-rubber coating\n\nexpandable, highly flexible, self-extinguishing, UL-certified\n\nBIS EXP-230 is used to fit around and protect components that vary widely in size.\n\n| Certification: | UL 1441\n\n| Temperature Range Min.: | -70 °C\n\n| Temperature Range Max.: | 235 °C",
