    "metaDescription": "Eine weitere WordPress-Website",
    "body": "## ELECTRICAL INSULATION; THERMAL, ABRASION AND VIBRATION PROTECTION\n\nBIT offers a comprehensive portfolio of premier-quality products for companies both in the conventional energy industry and in the renewable energy sector. Most of our products are certified according to worldwide industry standards and specifications (such as UL 224, UL 1441, and DIN IEC 60684). This makes them suitable for even the most demanding applications.\n\nBIT parts are, for instance, used in generators, transformers, wind turbines and plants, photovoltaic and solar plants, as well as electric actuators and motors. They also play a major role in cable and wiring loom and harness assembly. Our parts provide electrical insulation or serve as abrasion, anti-rattle or thermal protection.\n\nLet us empower your project with our high-quality products!\n\nPARTS OFTEN USED IN ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING\n\nBPMW\n\nPolyolefin\n\nhigh shrink ratio, medium wall thickness, UV-resistant\n\nBPMW heat-shrink tubing comes with exceptional mechanical properties.\n\n| Shrinking Rate: | 3:1\n\n| Temperature Range Min.: | -55 °C\n\n| Temperature Range Max.: | 110 °C\n\n### Polyolefin\n\nflame-retardant, high shrink ratio, adhesive-lined, practically non-flammable, UL-certified\n\nBPDW 100 permits flexible moisture-resistant insulation of cables and wires.\n\n| Shrinking Rate: | 3:1\n\n| Certification: | UL 224 (except clear-colored)\n\n| Temperature Range Min.: | -55 °C\n\n| Temperature Range Max.: | 125 °C\n\n### FKM\n\nflame-retardant, flexible, high chemical resistance, high temperature resistance\n\nBP VIT serves to protect components from high temperatures and corrosive fluids.\n\n| Shrinking Rate: | 2:1\n\n| Temperature Range Min.: | -55 °C\n\n| Temperature Range Max.: | +200 °C\n\n### Fiberglass with silicone-rubber coating\n\nexpandable, highly flexible, self-extinguishing, UL-certified\n\nBIS EXP-230 is used to fit around and protect components that vary widely in size.\n\n| Certification: | UL 1441\n\n| Temperature Range Min.: | -70 °C\n\n| Temperature Range Max.: | 235 °C",
